WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.310
A grey picture is not a thing with a name.

2
00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:06.310
On the computer it is a grid of

3
00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:09.030
numbers, one brightness in each cell.

4
00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:13.530
Today: pictures as grids, and what a

5
00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:15.610
small filter actually mixes.

6
00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:19.240
A grey image is one grid.

7
00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:23.030
A colour image is three, and each cell

8
00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:25.330
is a brightness, not an object.

9
00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:28.770
A three by three filter lays on the

10
00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:31.030
picture and multiplies nine cells.

11
00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:34.050
It writes that sum as the new pixel.

12
00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:37.710
An upright-edge filter lights walls.

13
00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:41.370
A blur averages neighbours, and neither

14
00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:43.050
knows it is looking at a face.

15
00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.540
Here is one position of the filter.

16
00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:49.710
Nine multiplications become one

17
00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:51.570
number, and the name of the

18
00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:53.570
object is not in that number.

19
00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:55.330
Quick check!

20
00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:57.790
A grey picture on a

21
00:00:57.790 --> 00:00:59.630
computer is which of these?

22
00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:01.850
A grid of numbers.

23
00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:05.490
Names, if they appear, come from many

24
00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:07.450
layers, not from one filter.

25
00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:11.450
In the app, open the convolution lab.

26
00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:15.390
Slide an edge filter and a blur, and

27
00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:17.190
say what each new picture shows.

28
00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:19.250
Your turn.

29
00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:22.390
Does a three by three filter already

30
00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:24.010
know it is looking at a face?

31
00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:26.140
Remember this.

32
00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:28.540
A filter mixes neighbours.

33
00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.360
It does not name what it sees.

34
00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:34.020
Try it on paper tonight.

35
00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:36.740
Sketch a three by three edge filter

36
00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:38.980
and compute one output pixel.
